{"type": "step", "node_id": 23, "parent_node_id": 22, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\nPlace the triangle in coordinates: $B=(0,0)$, $C=(14,0)$. From $AB=13$, $AC=15$:\n$$x^2+y^2=169,\\quad (x-14)^2+y^2=225 \\implies x=5,\\; y=12.$$\nSo $A=(5,12)$.\n\n**Circumcenter $O$:** The perpendicular bisector of $BC$ is $x=7$. The perpendicular bisector of $AB$ (midpoint $(2.5,6)$, slope $-5/12$) gives at $x=7$: $y=6-\\frac{5}{12}\\cdot 4.5=\\frac{33}{8}$. Thus $O=\\left(7,\\frac{33}{8}\\right)$.\n\n**Orthocenter $H$:** The altitude from $A$ is $x=5$. The altitude from $B$ has slope $\\frac{3}{4}$ (perpendicular to $AC$ of slope $-\\frac{4}{3}$), so $y=\\frac{3}{4}x$. At $x=5$: $y=\\frac{15}{4}$. Thus $H=\\left(5,\\frac{15}{4}\\right)$.\n\n**Circumcircle of $\\triangle AOH$:** Write $x^2+y^2+Dx+Ey+F=0$. Substituting $A$, $H$, $O$:\n\n- From $A$: $169+5D+12E+F=0$.\n- From $H$: $\\frac{625}{16}+5D+\\frac{15}{4}E+F=0$. Subtracting: $-\\frac{2079}{16}-\\frac{33}{4}E=0 \\implies E=-\\frac{63}{4}$.\n- From $O$: $\\frac{4225}{64}+7D+\\frac{33}{8}E+F=0$. Subtracting $A$'s equation: $-\\frac{6591}{64}+2D-\\frac{63}{8}E=0$. With $E=-\\frac{63}{4}$: $2D=-\\frac{1347}{64}\\implies D=-\\frac{1347}{128}$.\n- Then $F=\\frac{9295}{128}$.\n\nThe circle is:\n$$x^2+y^2-\\frac{1347}{128}x-\\frac{63}{4}y+\\frac{9295}{128}=0.$$\n\n**Intersection with $AB$:** Parametrize $P=A+t(B-A)=(5-5t,\\,12-12t)$, so $AP=13t$. Substituting:\n$$169t^2-\\frac{12337}{128}t=0.$$\nSince $12337=169\\times 73$, the nonzero root is $t_D=\\frac{73}{128}$, giving\n$$AD=13\\cdot\\frac{73}{128}=\\frac{949}{128}.$$\n\n**Intersection with $AC$:** Parametrize $P=A+s(C-A)=(5+9s,\\,12-12s)$, so $AP=15s$. Substituting:\n$$225s^2-\\frac{13275}{128}s=0.$$\nSince $13275=225\\times 59$, the nonzero root is $s_E=\\frac{59}{128}$, giving\n$$AE=15\\cdot\\frac{59}{128}=\\frac{885}{128}.$$\n\n**Ratio:**\n$$\\frac{AD}{AE}=\\frac{949/128}{885/128}=\\frac{949}{885}.$$\nCheck $\\gcd$: $949=13\\times 73$ and $885=3\\times 5\\times 59$, which are coprime. So $m=949$, $n=885$.\n\n$$m-n = 949-885 = \\boxed{64}.$$\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this geometry problem.\n\nTriangle ABC with AB=13, BC=14, CA=15. O circumcenter, H orthocenter. Circumcircle of triangle AOH intersects AB at D and AC at E. Find AD/AE = m/n, then m-n.\n\nFirst, let me set up coordinates. The 13-14-15 triangle. Let me place it conveniently.\n\nLet me use the standard placement. Place B at origin, C at (14, 0). Then A is at some point with AB=13, AC=15.\n\nA = (x, y) where x² + y² = 169 and (x-14)² + y² = 225.\nx² - 28x + 196 + y² = 225\n169 - 28x + 196 = 225\n365 - 28x = 225\n28x = 140\nx = 5\ny² = 169 - 25 = 144, y = 12.\n\nSo A = (5, 12), B = (0, 0), C = (14, 0).\n\nCircumcenter O: perpendicular bisector of BC is x = 7. \nPerpendicular bisector of AB: midpoint (2.5, 6), slope of AB = 12/5, so perp slope = -5/12.\nLine: y - 6 = -5/12 (x - 2.5). At x = 7: y - 6 = -5/12 (4.5) = -22.5/12 = -1.875. y = 4.125 = 33/8.\n\nSo O = (7, 33/8).\n\nOrthocenter H: altitude from A perpendicular to BC (horizontal) is x = 5. Altitude from B perpendicular to AC. Slope of AC = (0-12)/(14-5) = -12/9 = -4/3. Perp slope = 3/4. Line through B: y = 3x/4. At x = 5: y = 15/4.\n\nSo H = (5, 15/4).\n\nNote A = (5, 12), H = (5, 15/4). So AH is vertical line x = 5. Makes sense since altitude from A is vertical.\n\nNow circumcircle of AOH. Let me find it.\n\nA = (5, 12), O = (7, 33/8), H = (5, 15/4).\n\nGeneral circle: x² + y² + Dx + Ey + F = 0.\n\nFor A: 25 + 144 + 5D + 12E + F = 0 → 169 + 5D + 12E + F = 0\nFor H: 25 + 225/16 + 5D + (15/4)E + F = 0 → 25 + 225/16 = 625/16. So 625/16 + 5D + 15E/4 + F = 0\nFor O: 49 + 1089/64 + 7D + (33/8)E + F = 0 → 49 + 1089/64 = 3136/64 + 1089/64 = 4225/64. So 4225/64 + 7D + 33E/8 + F = 0\n\nSubtract A from H:\n625/16 - 169 + (15/4 - 12)E = 0\n625/16 - 2704/16 = -2079/16\n15/4 - 12 = 15/4 - 48/4 = -33/4\nSo -2079/16 - 33E/4 = 0 → 33E/4 = -2079/16 → E = -2079/16 · 4/33 = -2079/(16·33/4)... let me compute: E = -2079/16 × (4/33) = -2079·4/(16·33) = -8316/528 = -2079/132 = -693/44 = -63/4.\n\nWait let me recompute. -2079/16 = -33E/4 → E = -2079/16 × 4/33 = -2079×4/(16×33) = -8316/528. Simplify: 8316/528. 528 = 16×33. 8316 = 2079×4 = 2079×4. 2079/33 = 63. So 8316/528 = 63×4/16 = 252/16 = 63/4. So E = -63/4.\n\nSubtract A from O:\n4225/64 - 169 + (7-5)D + (33/8 - 12)E = 0\n4225/64 - 10816/64 = -6591/64\n2D + (33/8 - 96/8)E = 2D - 63E/8\nSo -6591/64 + 2D - 63E/8 = 0\nE = -63/4, so -63E/8 = -63×(-63/4)/8 = 63²/(4×8) = 3969/32\n-6591/64 + 2D + 3969/32 = 0\n3969/32 = 7938/64\n-6591/64 + 7938/64 = 1347/64\n2D = -1347/64 → D = -1347/128\n\nNow F from A's equation: 169 + 5D + 12E + F = 0\n5D = -6735/128\n12E = -756/4 = -63×12/4 = -189 = -24192/128\n169 = 21632/128\n21632/128 - 6735/128 - 24192/128 + F = 0\n(21632 - 6735 - 24192)/128 = -9295/128\nF = 9295/128\n\nCircle: x² + y² - (1347/128)x - (63/4)y + 9295/128 = 0.\n\nNow find intersection with AB and AC.\n\nLine AB: from A(5,12) to B(0,0). Parametrize: P = A + t(B - A) = (5-5t, 12-12t), t from 0 to 1. At t=0 it's A, t=1 it's B. AD corresponds to some t value, D = A + t_D(B-A), AD = t_D · AB = 13 t_D.\n\nLine AC: from A(5,12) to C(14,0). P = A + s(C - A) = (5+9s, 12-12s), s from 0 to 1. AE = s_E · AC = 15 s_E.\n\nSubstitute AB parametrization into circle:\nx = 5-5t, y = 12-12t.\nx² = (5-5t)² = 25 - 50t + 25t²\ny² = (12-12t)² = 144 - 288t + 144t²\nx² + y² = 169 - 338t + 169t²\n-(1347/128)x = -(1347/128)(5-5t) = -6735/128 + 6735t/128\n-(63/4)y = -(63/4)(12-12t) = -189 + 189t\n+9295/128\n\nSum = 0:\n169 - 338t + 169t² - 6735/128 + 6735t/128 - 189 + 189t + 9295/128 = 0\n\nConstant: 169 - 189 + (-6735 + 9295)/128 = -20 + 2560/128 = -20 + 20 = 0. Good, t=0 is a root (point A).\n\nt coefficient: -338 + 6735/128 + 189 = -149 + 6735/128 = (-149×128 + 6735)/128 = (-19072 + 6735)/128 = -12337/128\nt² coefficient: 169\n\nSo 169t² - (12337/128)t = 0 → t(169t - 12337/128) = 0.\nt_D = 12337/(128×169) = 12337/21512.\n\nLet me simplify. 21512 = 128 × 169. 12337 = ? Let me check gcd. 12337 / 169 = 73.0... 169 × 73 = 12337. Yes! So t_D = 169×73/(128×169) = 73/128.\n\nSo AD = 13 × 73/128 = 949/128.\n\nNow AC parametrization: x = 5+9s, y = 12-12s.\nx² = 25 + 90s + 81s²\ny² = 144 - 288s + 144s²\nx² + y² = 169 - 198s + 225s²\n-(1347/128)x = -(1347/128)(5+9s) = -6735/128 - 12123s/128\n-(63/4)y = -(63/4)(12-12s) = -189 + 189t... wait s. = -189 + 189s\n+9295/128\n\nSum: 169 - 198s + 225s² - 6735/128 - 12123s/128 - 189 + 189s + 9295/128 = 0\n\nConstant: 169 - 189 + 2560/128 = -20 + 20 = 0. Good, s=0 is root.\n\ns coefficient: -198 - 12123/128 + 189 = -9 - 12123/128 = (-1152 - 12123)/128 = -13275/128\ns² coefficient: 225\n\nSo 225s² - (13275/128)s = 0 → s(225s - 13275/128) = 0.\ns_E = 13275/(128×225) = 13275/28800. Simplify: divide by 75: 177/384. Divide by 3: 59/128.\n\nSo s_E = 59/128.\n\nAE = 15 × 59/128 = 885/128.\n\nAD/AE = (949/128)/(885/128) = 949/885.\n\ngcd(949, 885): 949 - 885 = 64. 885 = 13×64 + 53. 64 = 1×53 + 11. 53 = 4×11 + 9. 11 = 1×9 + 2. 9 = 4×2 + 1. So gcd = 1.\n\nSo m/n = 949/885, m - n = 949 - 885 = 64.\n\nLet me verify the computation of t_D and s_E once more.\n\nFor AB: 169t² - (12337/128)t = 0. t_D = 12337/(128·169). 12337 = 169 × 73? 169 × 70 = 11830, 169 × 73 = 11830 + 507 = 12337. Yes. So t_D = 73/128. AD = 13 · 73/128 = 949/128. ✓\n\nFor AC: 225s² - (13275/128)s = 0. s_E = 13275/(128·225). 13275/225 = 59. So s_E = 59/128. AE = 15·59/128 = 885/128. ✓\n\nAD/AE = 949/885. gcd(949,885): 949 = 13×73. 885 = 3×5×59. No common factors. So m=949, n=885, m-n=64.\n\nThe answer is 64.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786638742}
